.TH LINDA-SAY 1 2026-11-18 Linda "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linda-say \- speak a text through Linda's speech and audio, then exit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linda-say
.RI [ options ] " text"
.br
.B linda say
.RI [ options ] " text"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linda say
speaks the text after its options through Linda's speech and audio, waits until it has been heard,
and exits.
It reads the synthesizer and its settings from your Linda configuration and never changes it.
It starts nothing else of Linda, so it runs beside any screen reader already speaking.
.B linda-say
is the same as
.BR "linda say" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-synth " name"
Choose the synthesizer, such as espeak or openevv.
.TP
.BI \-\-voice " identifier"
Choose the voice, as \-\-list\-voices names it.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " number" "\fR, \fP" \-\-pitch " number" "\fR, \fP" \-\-volume " number"
Set the synthesizer's own settings, each a whole number from 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI \-\-gain " number"
Scale every sound it makes by a number from 0 to 1; 1 when not given.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Play to an output that makes no sound, to check everything else.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-voices
List the voices of the synthesizer, one to a line, and speak nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-sounds
Play Linda's start sound, a short beep and its error sound after the text.
.TP
.B \-\-factory
Ignore your configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-path " directory"
Read the configuration in this directory instead of yours.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
How long to wait for speech to finish; 30 when not given.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Say all this and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The text was heard.
.TP
.B 1
An unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
A mistake in what it was given.
.TP
.B 3
The synthesizer did not load.
.TP
.B 4
Nothing could be heard.
.TP
.B 5
Speech did not finish in time.
.TP
.B 6
Stopped by Control C.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linda (1)
